  "notes": "A simple bounce dance alongside the separate Hip_Dance. One intact character drawing provides a rigid head and complete clothing/limb joins. A smooth six-pixel upper-body rise eases into unchanged shoe contacts; alternating 1.5-pixel vertical hand bops use a continuous spatial mapping, without cutout joints, crossfades or model-size changes. The full head translates without stretching. Forty-eight rendered frames at30fps form two gentle beats over1600ms; duplicate poses share atlas cells. Hip_Dance remains a separate active clip. This is a simple planted bounce, not a stepping or hip-sway routine. Scale v6: one fixed whole-character transform per clip, matched to the standing-idle median opaque head silhouette area. It includes eyes/mouth, so blinking does not change the scale estimate. No frame-specific scaling, head/body cuts, or pose-height normalization. Grounded contacts remain y592; flight clearance is transformed about the shared root. Pose projection, breathing and original drawing proportions remain intact.",
  "source": "animations/27-intro-dance-lu-dance-hipmove/spritesheet-optimized-v1.png"
}
